--- A: pure pursuit helper + unchanged cap ---
-- Fixture fix A (Nox run-6 ruling): the contact leg pursues the proxy's CURRENT lane position instead of driving back
-- along the ego's own projection. Closing speed is clamp(proxy+8,12,60); the 40 studs/s^2 force cap is unchanged.
function Server.pursuitAcceleration(loop,targetS,position,velocity,speed)
 local lane=Sim.frame(loop.poly,targetS)
 local forward=Vector3.new(lane.LookVector.X,0,lane.LookVector.Z).Unit
 local right=Vector3.new(-forward.Z,0,forward.X)
 local acc=forward*math.clamp((speed-velocity:Dot(forward))*2,-38,10)+right*math.clamp((lane.Position-position):Dot(right)*1.5-velocity:Dot(right)*2,-12,12)
 if acc.Magnitude>40 then acc=acc.Unit*40 end
 return acc,lane
end
-- Fixture fix C (Nox run-6 ruling): both named fail-fast guards for the contact leg. Pure, so the offline spec can pin
-- them; nil means the leg is still valid. A reached contact (touches>0) is never overridden by these guards.
function Server.contactLegGuard(distance,touches,sinceContactDrive)
